{
	title: 'Drafts that follow you, and optimistic sending',
	spec: 'Typed text is never lost (tasks/j1/states.md, Drafts and sending). Each session has one draft stored on the host, so a prompt started in the terminal can be finished on the phone; clients keep a local copy (a file for the terminal, localStorage for the web) and sync it when connected, so typing while disconnected is safe too. A sent prompt shows at once, marked pending until the host acknowledges its command id; while disconnected it stays pending and is sent on reconnect, never twice, and the draft is cleared only after the acknowledgement. Reference: the old draft.ts (artifact). Every draft command the host accepts is answered with the resulting draft, also when it changed nothing (the host already held that text), so the edit of a client always settles and is never resent in a loop. Test the loss cases: host restart while typing, disconnect then send, client crash before acknowledgement, and a draft equal to the one the host holds.',
	status: 'done',
	needs: ['r6'],
	notes: [
		'Host: src/host/drafts.ts keeps sessions/<id>/draft.ason { text, rev } (liveFile, saved before the answer). Protocol: command draft { sessionId, text, base? }, event draft { sessionId, draft: { text, rev }, command? } naming the command id that changed it, snapshot.draft (absent until first changed). draft is in host `once`, so a resent draft id is not applied twice.',
		'Conflicts: a draft whose base is not the current rev keeps both texts (current + blank line + new) unless one contains the other; nothing is ever dropped. The host clears the draft (host.sent) when it accepts a submit, steering and queued ones included, whose text contains the whole draft, and broadcasts it with the submit id.',
		"Client: src/common/drafts.ts is shared by terminal and page (defaults: connection.send, nextId, pending). One draft command in flight per session; edits meanwhile go in the next after the ack. Local { text, base, dirty, sending[] }: on a snapshot a dirty local copy wins and is sent; otherwise the host's replaces it.",
		'Optimistic send: drafts.submit empties the editor at once and keeps { id, text } in `sending` (and in the store) until ack; a crashed client resends it on the next snapshot with the same id, and the host (host.submitted, history `command`) acks without a second submit. A rejected submit goes back into the editor, before text typed since.',
		"Stores: terminal src/client/draft-file.ts, state/drafts/<id>.ason (dir set in main.ts); page localStorage `hal-draft:<id>`. Several terminals on one machine write the same file (temp file per pid); their content comes from the same host draft, but one terminal's unacknowledged prompt can be overwritten by another's save before a crash. Rare; per-process files would fix it.",
		'transcript.fold must ignore `draft` events (else they fall through to the turn-end branch); new event types need adding there.',
		"Web drafts, from the old Hal (commit ae57750, docs/web.md 'Drafts are sacred', artifact tasks/1b/old-web.md): write localStorage synchronously on every input event and again on pagehide and visibilitychange (iOS evicts backgrounded pages without warning); if a write throws (quota, private mode) keep the text in memory and show it is not saved; after a send clears only when the box still holds exactly what was sent."
	]
